{
  "slug": "ordered-payout",
  "title": "Ordered payout queue: one authenticated continuation step",
  "kind": "coin_puzzle",
  "security_scope": "Original WIP teaching policy for issue #16, not ready for real funds. A funded instance curries one proper list (its own module hash, the digest of the remaining queue). Each spend opens the head as sha256(domain || recipient || next), pays that recipient exactly 1000 mojos and, unless next is the queue's terminal digest, recreates the same module curried with next and the remaining funds. The spender supplies the coin's amount and ASSERT_MY_AMOUNT makes consensus check it; a nonterminal step requires at least two payouts and the final step exactly one. With correct funding (amount equal to 1000 mojos times the queue length, and a module field naming the selected artifact, both checked by the host before funding) no spender can skip, reorder, inject or end early. Advancement is permissionless; nothing guarantees anyone advances the queue, inclusion, cross-block atomicity, or recovery of funds from a mis-funded instance.",
  "environment": "strict",
  "reference_mode": "module",
  "provenance": {
    "classification": "original teaching implementation",
    "references": [
      "https://chialisp.com/conditions/",
      "https://chialisp.com/chialisp-currying/",
      "https://github.com/judeallred/chialisp-oxide/issues/16"
    ],
    "source_origin": "All four paired source files (Rust export, independent Chialisp reference, Rue port and Python oracle) are original implementations of this explicit teaching contract. It is a new policy built on the reviewed chialisp_oxide::continuation helpers, not a re-port of the retained batch-one, batch-two or spuds experiments.",
    "limitations": [
      "One fixed 1000-mojo payout per spend; no reserve, fee, refund or abort branch. Funds stay committed until valid steps are advanced.",
      "Funding correctness is a host preflight. An instance funded with the wrong amount or a module field that does not name the selected artifact can become permanently stuck; the puzzle cannot detect either before it is spent.",
      "Consensus prevents spending a coin twice, but a third party can race or accelerate a valid step. It cannot change the recipients, order or amounts.",
      "SHA-256 collision and preimage resistance are assumptions. Proof models do not cover SHA, this export or the multi-coin chain."
    ]
  },
